        "node_id": "n_2_7ae00f",
        "thought_text": "The current implementation uses Python's built-in float type, which can lead to precision loss for very large numbers. To avoid this issue, we should implement our own custom algorithm for handling large numbers as strings and perform the exponentiation and normalization manually. This approach will allow us to maintain precision for arbitrarily large numbers.",
